2. Core Functional Modules
 * Module 1: Stellar-Magnetospheric Ingestion & Coupling (\mathcal{M}_{\text{sol}})
   * Inputs: Real-time SDO (AIA/HMI), Parker Solar Probe (FIELDS/WISPR), and SOHO/LASCO telemetry streams.
   * Functions: Resolves coronal magnetic field topologies, Alfvén critical surface crossings, and interplanetary magnetic field (IMF) polarity shifts to compute dayside reconnection rates and magnetopause compression metrics.
 * Module 2: Lithospheric Induction & Crustal Stress Solver (\mathcal{M}_{\text{crust}})
   * Inputs: Magnetospheric current surge indices and lithospheric conductivity grids (\text{CMB-CRU-003}).
   * Functions: Executes magnetohydrodynamic (MHD) induction models to calculate telluric current distributions and thermal-mechanical stress tensors across continental fault systems.
 * Module 3: Global Hazard & Weathering Cascade Engine (\mathcal{M}_{\text{hazard}})
   * Inputs: Coronal Mass Ejection (CME) shockwave parameters and Universal Planetary Hazard Engine (UPHE) fields.
   * Functions: Computes ionospheric density perturbations, atmospheric stripping rates, and precipitation anomalies, directly mapping how space weather alters local water activity (a_{\text{H}_2\text{O}}) and thermal boundaries (\mathcal{I}_{\text{thermo}}).
 * Module 4: Paragenetic & Anthropogenic Mineral Genesis (\mathcal{M}_{\text{min}})
   * Inputs: Environmental parameter vectors (\mathbf{E}_{\text{env}}) and industrial activity datasets (\mathcal{I}_{\text{ind}}).
   * Functions: Dynamically updates the Planetary Mineralogical Paragenesis transition weight matrix (\mathbf{W}) and executes classical nucleation solvers (K_{\text{kin}}) to forecast both deep-time and anthropogenic mineral phase evolution across planetary crusts.
 * Module 5: Star-Coupled Telemetry & Provenance Network (\mathcal{M}_{\text{tele}})
   * Inputs: Continuous-variable (CV) squeezed-light states and distributed sensor arrays.
   * Functions: Maintains zero-latency state synchronization across stellar-planetary baselines via VANGUARD-LITE protocols, binding every runtime state vector and output artifact to authorship design standard CMB-0001.
